VALUES ('New support, helpdesk and advice for community groups from Department', 'new-support-helpdesk-and-advice-for-community-groups-from-department', '<p>Last week, the government published a national action plan, including details on support for a community response to Covid-19. There is quite a lot of detail in this plan that may be helpful to community groups.</p>
<p>Link: <a href="https://communityworkireland.us14.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f9396b10cc05b70c128f75334&amp;id=42fd12a849&amp;e=3895580dba">https://www.gov.ie/en/publication/70be56-government-action-plan-for-community-response-to-covid-19/</a></p>
<p>The National Action Plan was published on March 16<sup>th</sup> and set out “a whole-of-society response and mobilisation of resources across Government and society to fight the spread of the virus”.</p>
<p>This week, the Department  published a six-page information leaflet to support the community response to Coronavirus: “You, Your Community and COVID-19” focuses on our public health duties and gives advice on to groups and to individuals about volunteering.</p>
<p>Link: <a href="https://mcusercontent.com/c722bbb106ff348118090b624/files/61cafd71-f9fe-41ba-80c5-2b9bdaea2089/YouYourCommunityandCORVID1020MarchOnWEbsite.pdf">https://mcusercontent.com/c722bbb106ff348118090b624/files/61cafd71-f9fe-41ba-80c5-2b9bdaea2089/YouYourCommunityandCORVID1020MarchOnWEbsite.pdf</a></p>
<p>The leaflet advised people they could volunteer through the Department-supported network of volunteer offices.</p>
<p>It noted that some volunteers may need to be Garda vetted and that this process would be speeded up and people volunteering in connection with Covid-19 would be prioritised.</p>
<p>The document was emailed out as part of a pack covering public health advice, do’s and don’ts of sensible volunteering, advice specifically for community groups, and tips on guarding against fraud and generating trust.</p>
<p>Resources cover:</p>
<p>&#8211; ‘How can I volunteer?’</p>
<p>&#8211; ‘Sensible volunteering – Do’s and Don’ts’</p>
<p>&#8211; ‘Advice for local community groups – how can we get volunteers?’</p>
<p>&#8211; ‘Advice for vulnerable people who need supports’</p>
<p>&#8211; ‘How to guard against fraud and generate trust’</p>
<p><em>(Links to follow &#8211; in the meantime, we recommend you visit www.volunteer.ie where there is advice for both formal and <a href="https://www.volunteer.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Informal-Volunteering-Guide.pdf">i</a><a href="https://www.volunteer.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Informal-Volunteering-Guide.pdf">nformal volunteering initiatives</a> and <a href="https://www.volunteer.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Volunteering-During-an-Emergency-What-to-Expect.pdf">volunteering during an emergency</a>).<br />
</em></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Volunteering_During_COVID-19_v2.jpg" alt="" width="956" height="296" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Volunteering_During_COVID-19_v2.jpg 956w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Volunteering_During_COVID-19_v2-300x93.jpg 300w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Volunteering_During_COVID-19_v2-768x238.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 956px) 100vw, 956px" /></p>
<p>The Department of Rural and Community Development has also opened a dedicated helpdesk contactable by email to assist community groups seeking advice or with queries. The email helpdesk is open 7 days a week. It is: c&amp;vsupports@drcd.gov.ie</p>
<p>The Department reminds everyone that the HSE website is the key source for health advice: www.hse.ie/coronavirus.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h3>PUBLIC HEALTH UPDATES</h3>
<p>On the public health response to Covid-19, a digital pack has been issued and it can be downloaded at: <a href="https://www.hse.ie/eng/services/news/newsfeatures/covid19-updates/partner-resources/">https://www.hse.ie/eng/services/news/newsfeatures/covid19-updates/partner-resources/</a></p>
<p>As part of the national response to Covid-19, the Department of Health, the Department of Rural and Community Development and the HSE are working closely to support stakeholders and community groups. The latest updates include the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>There is now a video on social distancing: <a href="https://communityworkireland.us14.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f9396b10cc05b70c128f75334&amp;id=3183c387bb&amp;e=3895580dba">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I0-uuijhF4Q</a></li>
<li>Translated resources in 10 languages can be found at: <a href="https://communityworkireland.us14.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f9396b10cc05b70c128f75334&amp;id=3e1c9bb3ba&amp;e=3895580dba">https://www.hse.ie/eng/services/news/newsfeatures/covid19-updates/partner-resources/covid-19-translated-resources/</a></li>
<li>Social distancing graphics for premises floors can be found here: <a href="https://communityworkireland.us14.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f9396b10cc05b70c128f75334&amp;id=d6f681b568&amp;e=3895580dba">https://www.gov.ie/en/publication/472f64-covid-19-coronavirus-guidance-and-advice/#social-distancing-graphics</a></li>
</ul>
<p>More updates are planned for early next week. Meanwhile, the Covid-19 Health Communications Stakeholder Support says that it will respond to urgent concerns. It says: “We would be grateful if you would let us know if your organisation has any specific requests or urgent needs in relation to Coronavirus COVID-19 public health information materials. If you do, please email us at <a href="mailto:Partner.Pack@hse.ie">Partner.Pack@hse.ie</a> to let us know.”</p>', 'There has been a surge in people volunteering and the Government and the Department of Rural and Community Development has issued guidance and advice to volunteers and community groups.', 'https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/volunteerism-CVus2.jpg', '', '[{"slug":"activism-volunteering","title":"Activism & Volunteering"},{"slug":"community","title":"Community"}]', '[{"slug":"changingireland","title":"#ChangingIreland"},{"slug":"communityresponseirl","title":"#CommunityResponseIRL"},{"slug":"department-rural-community-development-drcd","title":"Department of Rural and Community Development"}]', '', 248975, 1, '2020-03-24T14:21:47Z', '2020-03-24T14:30:09Z', '2020-03-24T14:21:47Z')
